{"seq":83,"data":{"type":"RUN_FINISHED","threadId":"f24f2e73-13a3-427a-a4a1-a89a6c75372c","runId":"run_1_1788525896241","result":"Done! I've created `/app/run.py` with the `run_tasks` function. Here's how it works:\n\n**Key features:**\n- **Semaphore-based concurrency control**: Limits tasks to `max_concurrent` running at once\n- **Graceful interrupt handling**: When you press Ctrl+C, the function:\n  1. Catches the `KeyboardInterrupt`\n  2. Cancels all pending tasks (injecting `CancelledError`)\n  3. Waits for all tasks to finish (allowing `try/finally` and context managers to run cleanup)\n  4. Re-raises the interrupt\n\nThis ensures that even if interrupted, each task's cleanup code (in `finally` blocks or async context managers) will execute before the program exits.\n\nYou can use it like:\n```python\nfrom run import run_tasks\n\nasync def some_task():\n    try:\n        # do work\n        pass\n    finally:\n        # cleanup code always runs\n        pass\n\nawait run_tasks([some_task, another_task], max_concurrent=5)\n```","rawEvent":{"duration_api_ms":17033,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f24f2e73-13a3-427a-a4a1-a89a6c75372c","total_cost_usd":0.018517850000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":17,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2827,"cache_read_input_tokens":26631,"output_tokens":2239,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1599},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2827},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":8,"output_tokens":288,"cache_read_input_tokens":13720,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2018,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2018,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":1024,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.001109,"contextWindow":